1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Length of Last Word — LeetCode 58

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,200
Problem: given a string of words separated by spaces, return the length of the last word.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,400
Example: s = "a moon" with trailing spaces. The last word is "moon", so the answer is 4.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,600
Note the trailing spaces don't count toward the word.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,600
Key idea: why scan the whole string forward? The last word is at the END.

6
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,600
So walk backwards — skip the trailing spaces first, then count letters until the next space.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:26,000
Start i at the last index with len = 0. While s[i] is a space, decrement i.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Two trailing spaces get skipped, and now i lands on the letter n.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,500
Now while s[i] is a letter, count it and step left: n, o, o, m — len reaches 4.

10
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:37,500
The next character is the space before the word, so we stop. len = 4.

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,500
Bonus, cleaner code: find the last non-space, then the last space before it — one expression.

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,500
Either way we only ever touch the last word. Time O(n), space O(1).

13
